# The root of an area's tree folds the whole of it.
#
# Everything observed in an area hangs under its card from one root symbol, on the first row under
# the card. A click on it puts the whole of that area's tree away — every element, every thought,
# every waiting act — and another brings it back as it was. Like an element's own fold it is the
# screen's and not the game's: nothing is lost, lapsed or withdrawn, but nothing under it is drawn
# or answers a click while it is folded. A way's tree hangs from its line and is no area's.
#
# --grant-mm woodcraft --means-only woodcraft: examining is refused by an acting mind that does not
# also observe, and the script wants an act left waiting under the tree.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --auto-dialogue --location-type test --location-id 0 --start-area "Test Yard" --period dawn --grant-mm woodcraft --means-only woodcraft

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60
advance 12 180

# Nothing observed: no tree, and so no root.
expect-no-state symbols click root

# Two things of the yard are looked at, and one is thought into an act.
strategy succeed
goal examine
click observe thing
choose childhood_memory
advance 12 180
click observe thing
choose childhood_memory
advance 12 180
click think last
choose ripelore
advance 12 180
expect-state symbols click root "Test Yard"
expect-no-state symbols click root "Test Yard" (folded)
expect-state symbols click act 0

# Under the pointer the root says what a click does, on the clickable ground.
point root "Test Yard"
wait 1
expect-state pointer-label ground=yellow
expect-state pointer-label all I made of the test yard · fold

# Folded: the elements, their marks and the waiting act are put away, and still there.
click root "Test Yard"
expect-state symbols click root "Test Yard" (folded)
expect-no-state symbols element
expect-no-state symbols click act
expect-no-state symbols click think
expect-state trees area_folded=yes
expect-state trees act state=waiting
click act 0
point root "Test Yard"
wait 1
expect-state pointer-label · unfold

# What is not yet observed is not part of the tree: the card's own symbols still answer.
expect-state symbols click observe thing in "Test Yard"

# Unfolded: as it was.
click root "Test Yard"
expect-no-state trees area_folded=yes
expect-state symbols click act 0
expect-state symbols click think
quit
